# The flood, on the riverbank, before the Hollow Mouth (scripts/creature_prologue.gd reads this).
# Claude's draft lines for Preston, 2026-10-11. Edit freely: a line with a name and a colon is spoken,
# a line without one is narration; [#face] picks the portrait (happy, joyous, sad, worried, surprised,
# angry, determined); "- " lines are choices, and lines indented under a choice play only if it is picked.
# {{...}} fills in a name from the game. How we write: docs/design/dialogue-voice-guide.md.

~ start
if not chosen_by_soul
	The bank gives way under you, and the river comes up cold around your feet.
	You remember being human. Then you look down at yourself.
	- {{starter_0}}
		do pick_hero(0)
	- {{starter_1}}
		do pick_hero(1)
	- {{starter_2}}
		do pick_hero(2)
else
	The bank gives way under you, and the river comes up cold around your feet.
You remember being human. {{sense}}
Somebody's hollering over the rain. Two voices, up on the higher bank.
Whose voice do you answer?
- {{name_a}}
	do pick_partner(0)
- {{name_b}}
	do pick_partner(1)
{{partner_name}}: [#surprised] Hey! Hey, you alive down there?
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] Oh, thank goodness. I seen you laying in the mud and thought you were a log. Then the log blinked.
- I'm okay, I think.
	{{partner_name}}: [#happy] "I think" is good. I'll take "I think."
- Where am I?
	{{partner_name}}: [#surprised] Right under Highbank. Well, what's left of the bank. It's mostly river now.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] You picked a bad night to nap by the river, I'll tell you what.
{{partner_name}} is hugging something to its chest. A parcel, wrapped tight in oilcloth.
{{partner_name}}: [#sad] Oh, this? It's mail. The river took the whole mail shed right off its posts. This is the only one I could grab.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] I'm not even supposed to be out here. I'm not a runner yet. Starward won't let me run a route without a partner, and nobody wants to pair up with the trainee.
{{partner_name}}: [#worried] But I was laying there listening to it rain, and something just told me I needed to come down here tonight. Don't ask me what.
{{partner_name}}: [#surprised] ...And then there's you.
Thunder. A slab of the bank slumps into the water right behind you.
{{partner_name}}: [#surprised] Okay! Okay, nope. The road up's already under. We gotta get higher.
{{partner_name}}: [#determined] Stay right on my tail, alright? I'm not losing you and the mail both.
- Right behind you.
	{{partner_name}}: [#joyous] Ha! Okay. Partners for one night, at least.
- You won't lose me.
	{{partner_name}}: [#happy] Promise? 'Cause I'm gonna hold you to that.
=> END
